1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,799
<|startoftranscript|><|en|><|transcribe|><|0.00|> We are to hear Christ who has been appointed by the Father as our divine teacher.<|4.80|>

2
00:00:04,799 --> 00:00:09,800
<|4.80|> At the same time, Paul confirms our creed that Christ is very God.<|9.80|>

3
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:16,399
<|9.80|> That Christ is very God is apparent in that Paul ascribes to Him divine powers equally with the Father,<|16.40|>

4
00:00:16,399 --> 00:00:20,000
<|16.40|> as for instance the power to dispense grace and peace.<|20.00|>

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,799
<|20.00|> To bestow peace and grace lies in the province of God, who alone can create these blessings.<|25.80|>

6
00:00:25,799 --> 00:00:27,319
<|25.80|> The angels cannot.<|27.32|>

